cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "Investment-Viability Analysis"
abstract: >-
  Ingests a company's financials from SEC EDGAR filings or user supplied
  statements, computes standard finance ratios, valuation, and capital
  budgeting metrics, and produces a live formula Excel workbook and a
  narrative report with a viable, conditional, or not viable verdict.
  Educational analysis only, not investment, tax, or legal advice.
authors:
  - family-names: Esparza
    given-names: Mark
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-5171-102X"
repository-code: "https://github.com/mark-esparza/investment-viability-analysis"
url: "https://mark-esparza.github.io"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
keywords:
  - financial analysis
  - SEC EDGAR
  - valuation
  - capital budgeting
  - Excel
